            <div xml:id="d674">

                <pb facs="0680" n="564" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg564"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 365.117/282.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State ad
                            interim to Ambassador Page</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-06-10">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 10, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>256. Your 318, 8th. Enrico Ajello was born in New York City, March 15, 1882.
                    Father naturalized October 25, 1889. With exception short business trip Italy
                    1906, has resided continuously this country. Ask release, referring Department’s
                    telegram 7th concerning Ghiloni. Report. Ajello case previously taken up with
                    Consul Naples.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
